Scope XUDP GlobalID by TUN exit when per-exit UDP is enabled.

Without a scope the source hash and wire format stay byte-for-byte upstream.
With per-exit UDP, equal source-only IDs make different flows reuse one server
XUDP session (XUDP hit), detach the previous Mux and share its UDP socket. Add
the exit key to the hash so independent exits get independent UDP sessions.
Reconnecting the same exit retains its ID and can still reattach that session.

SOCKS and other inbounds are unchanged. PacketWriter and common/mux/frame.go
stay upstream: every nonzero GlobalID is written exactly as before.

